{"author":{"id":"f943aa1c5ee078b881a8e97535a4e2ccb401d01ca00f4128126befa9cca58a32"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792658210,"nonce":"stACnE+iZFKq/taNrUzyoK1dA/s=","title":"cycle: M3 to M6, plan with wtx, tests and checks, review, risk/code/verify screens","message":"The cycle protocol's M3 to M6 (docs/prd/cycle-protocol.md), after M1 and M2 landed with 7fd2891: the one page, the step bar, `[cycle]` criteria headings and kinds, the step buttons that move the status, each step's discussion, and Intent's criteria warnings.\n\n- **M3, step 3 with wtx:** Start opens the branch with `wtx go` in plan mode and a draft PR holding the plan; Revise goes through `wtx brief`; Approve takes the agent out of plan mode; `plans-in-pr` keeps plans out of PRs per project. Low risk starts the branch at step 4.\n- **M4, step 4, the tests and the checks:** `[cycle.tests.*]` suites and `[cycle.checks.*]`, proposed from lefthook, else the Makefile or package.json. git-board runs only the toml's argv; slow suites are CI's. Mark ready for review is gated on the server.\n- **M5, step 6, review:** the Changes view as the canvas's C6: threads sent to the agent, Approve and Request changes.\n- **M6, steps 2, 5 and 7:** C2's three risk options with the AI's suggestion; C5's commits and the PR's title and description; C7's checklist with who and when, and the run at the merged head.\n\nEach milestone gets its own branch. Out of scope: environments for e2e, reading CI results back, running CI locally, GB-21. The agent never decides pass or fail. Live checks go to guilbep/git-board-test or guilbep-sandbox only, never co2-calculator.\n\n\n- a normal-risk issue's Start opens a worktree and a draft PR with the plan, and Review unlocks when that PR is marked ready\n- the touched suites come pre-ticked, a fast suite runs in the worktree from the toml's argv, and a red check blocks Mark ready for review\n- a bug needs a test that fails before the fix, and a feature's criterion with no test is a warning\n- the page matches C6 at step 6\n- the pages match C2, C5 and C7\n- `make ci` and `cd web \u0026\u0026 npm run typecheck \u0026\u0026 npm test` pass for each milestone","files":null}]}